Chapter: OccurrenceCheck

 The shapes:

  - occ-dead:   a let bound and never used            -> Dead
  - occ-once:   a let used exactly once               -> Once
  - occ-many:   a let used twice                       -> Many
  - occ-arm:    a let used once in each if-arm         -> Many, NOT Once
                (the conservative join: arms are summed, so occurs-once
                inlining can never duplicate work into both arms)
  - occ-shadow: an inner and an outer let of one name  -> inner and
                outer classified independently (inner Many, outer Dead)
  - occ-act:    an act bind used in a later statement  -> the bind
                scopes over the statements after it

Section: Shapes

  occ-dead : Integer -> Integer
  occ-dead (n) = let u = n + 4 in n

  occ-once : Integer -> Integer
  occ-once (n) = let y = n + 2 in y + 5

  occ-many : Integer -> Integer
  occ-many (n) = let z = n + 3 in z + z

  occ-arm : Integer -> Integer
  occ-arm (n) = let x = n + 1 in if n == 0 then x else x + 6

  occ-shadow : Integer -> Integer
  occ-shadow (n) = let x = n + 7 in let x = n + 1 in x + x

  occ-act : Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  occ-act (n) = act
   a <- port-in-byte n
   b <- port-in-byte (a + 1)
   a + b
  end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni "ok"
  end

